# Touch look (drag-to-rotate camera)

## Overview

Hold-and-drag on the stream viewport rotates the camera (first-person look-around). Works with both mouse and touch. A quick tap (no drag) is treated as a pick/click request instead.

## Pipeline

```
Frontend (pointer drag on #remote-video)
  → sendCustomMessage('touchLookDelta', { dx, dy }) while dragging
  → sendCustomMessage('touchLookEnd', {}) on pointer-up after a drag
    → Kit: TouchLookHandler accumulates yaw/pitch deltas; arms release coast on end
      → PlayerInputController.update() → tick(dt) applies drag + exponential coast
        → camera RotateXYZ
```

### Frontend: `useRemoteVideoPointerGestures.ts`

Hook wired from `AppStream.tsx` / `StreamOnlyWindow` (not inline in `AppStream.tsx`).

- `DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX = 8` — drag must exceed 8 px before counting as a drag (avoids treating taps as look).
- `pointerdown`: captures pointer (left button only), records start position.
- `pointermove`: frame deltas `dx`, `dy`. If threshold exceeded, sends either:
  - **Placed camera**: `placedCameraRotate` with `{ cameraId, deltaYaw: -dx * 0.15, deltaPitch: -dy * 0.15 }`
  - **Stream drag** (FP or bird-eye): `touchLookDelta` with `{ dx, dy }` (invert applied when `invertTouchLook`)
- `pointerup`: after a drag on stream look (not placed-cam / vertex drag / map twist), sends **`touchLookEnd`** `{}`; if no drag, sends pick request (NDC, object-fit: cover).

### Kit: `TouchLookHandler`

**File:** `younite.usd_viewer_player_core_extension` → `inputs/point_click/touch_look_handler.py`

- Subscribes to **`touchLookDelta`** and **`touchLookEnd`** (Events 2.0; both registered via `register_event_alias`).
- Sensitivity: `0.15` (constructor default) — `yaw += -dx * sensitivity`, `pitch += dy * sensitivity`.
- **`ACTIVE_TIMEOUT_S = 0.15`** — recent delta ⇒ dragging; `is_active()` is also true during release coast (auto-mover defers path look-ahead while coast runs).
- **`tick(dt)`** — **first-person only** (called from `PlayerInputController`): applies drag deltas this frame, then optional **release coast** after `touchLookEnd`. Coast uses velocity from the last drag frame (`vel = delta / dt`) and exponential decay. **`dt`** must come from `PlayerUpdateLoop` → `event.payload["dt"]` (see `events-api.mdc` / `cct-movement.mdc`).
- **`tick_bird_eye_pan(dt)`** — **bird-eye pan** (called from `PlayerInputController`): drag deltas this frame, then a **very short** post-release coast after `touchLookEnd` (same event as FP; both coast flags arm together).

#### Release coast tuning (class constants in `touch_look_handler.py`)

| Constant | Default | Effect |
|----------|---------|--------|
| `COAST_DECAY_PER_SEC` | `12.0` | Lower = longer coast (was `22.5`, too short) |
| `COAST_STOP_VEL` | `0.25` | deg/s cutoff — coast ends below this |

Coast is armed only on **`touchLookEnd`** (not when the finger is held still without new deltas), so mid-drag pauses do not drift.

#### Bird-eye pan coast tuning (same file)

| Constant | Default | Effect |
|----------|---------|--------|
| `BIRD_EYE_COAST_DECAY_PER_SEC` | `95.0` | Higher = shorter coast |
| `BIRD_EYE_COAST_STOP_VEL` | `0.18` | analog units/s cutoff for forward/right coast |

Shared exponential decay: `inputs/point_click/ease_helpers.py` → `apply_exponential_coast`.

### Kit: `PlayerInputController.update()`

**File:** `younite.usd_viewer_player_core_extension` → `inputs/player_input_controller.py`

Merges multiple look sources (desktop mouse, Q/E keyboard, mobile joystick, touch look):

```
self._yaw  += t_yaw          # from tick(dt) in first-person (drag + coast)
self._pitch += -t_pitch       # negated
```

Final camera write: `RotateXYZ(pitch, yaw, 0)` in degrees, pitch clamped to ±89.

### Net sign mapping (default / direct mode)

| Action | dx/dy | Accumulated | Camera |
|--------|-------|-------------|--------|
| Drag right | dx > 0 | yaw -= dx × 0.15 | Camera turns right |
| Drag left | dx < 0 | yaw += \|dx\| × 0.15 | Camera turns left |
| Drag down | dy > 0 | pitch += dy × 0.15, then negated | Camera looks down |
| Drag up | dy < 0 | pitch -= \|dy\| × 0.15, then negated | Camera looks up |

## Invert toggle (mobile-natural scrolling)

For mobile-first UX, an **Invert Touch Look** toggle is available in dev mode under **Navigation → Touch Look Direction**.

When inverted, `dx` and `dy` are negated in `useRemoteVideoPointerGestures.ts` before sending to Kit. Effect: swipe right → look left (like dragging a map).

### State flow

```
StreamOnlyWindow.tsx
  invertTouchLook state (default false)
    → UIControls.tsx (toggle: Direct | Inverted)
    → AppStream.tsx prop → negates dx/dy when true
```

The toggle only appears in dev mode (`UIControls` is rendered when `appMode === 'dev'`). Default CU mode keeps direct mapping.

## Placed camera rotation

Placed cameras (`placed_cam_*`) use a separate message `placedCameraRotate` handled by `camera_placement_extension`:

- **Kit file:** `younite.camera_placement_extension` → `extension.py` → `_on_rotate`
- Adds `deltaYaw` / `deltaPitch` to stored orientation, clamps pitch to ±89, writes rotation.
- Invert toggle also applies to placed camera drag.

## Related: other look inputs

| Source | Message | Handler |
|--------|---------|---------|
| Mobile look joystick | `lookInput { yaw, pitch }` | `WebJoystickInput.set_look` → `player_input_controller.py` |
| Desktop mouse (Kit carb) | native carb mouse move | `keyboard_mouse_input.py` `_on_mouse_event` (sensitivity 0.1) |
| Viewport default gestures | disabled | `viewport_safety_extension` removes scroll zoom, RMB look, MMB pan |

## Bird-eye view: same `touchLookDelta` events, different consumer

When `viewType === "birdEye"`, `PlayerInputController.update()` uses **`tick_bird_eye_pan(dt)`** (not `tick(dt)`) to fill `movement_state["forward"]` / `["right"]` with sign inversion for "grab the world" panning. **`touchLookEnd`** arms bird-eye pan coast as well as FP look coast. Map **rotation** coast is separate (`birdEyeYawEnd` → `BirdEyeYawService`). See `bird-eye-map-controls.mdc`.

## Events (Web → Kit)

| Event | Payload | Consumer |
|-------|---------|----------|
| `touchLookDelta` | `{ dx, dy }` | `TouchLookHandler` — accumulate rotation |
| `touchLookEnd` | `{}` | `TouchLookHandler` — arm FP look coast + bird-eye pan coast |

